    ;; The module _lzma (queue 208; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, "As built: 208", "After the decisions"): CPython
    ;; 3.14.10's Modules/_lzmamodule.c (with Modules/clinic/_lzmamodule.c.h's argument parsing) ported statement for
    ;; statement over liblzma 5.2.5 itself, the C library built by ci's builder (arbace/clib/xz's node program) and called
    ;; through arbace/clib, as _bz2 is (arbace/pybz2: its notes on memory, the output blocks, the GIL and the finalizers
    ;; hold here too). LZMACompressor (formats XZ, ALONE, RAW; a preset or a filter chain), LZMADecompressor (AUTO, XZ,
    ;; ALONE, RAW; memlimit; check, eof, needs_input, unused_data), is_check_supported, _encode_filter_properties,
    ;; _decode_filter_properties, LZMAError and the constants. lzma.py (LZMAFile, lzma.open, compress, decompress) is
    ;; the tarball's Python over it.
    ;;
    ;; The filter specifiers (Python dicts) become liblzma's lzma_filter chains and option structures in C memory through
    ;; tools/pyi/clib/xz/pylzma.c's helpers (pylzma_chain, pylzma_lzma_new, pylzma_lzma_set, ...), which keep their layout
    ;; liblzma's; parse_filter_spec_*'s PyArg_ParseTupleAndKeywords over the dict is specArgs: a key not among the
    ;; filter's option names, or a value its converter refuses, is the "Invalid filter specifier" ValueError CPython
    ;; raises in place of the parser's error.


